/S /H3
/T (A robust semantic layer is vital for ensuring that all enterprise data is governed by consistent business definitions and metrics. This layer should comprehensively encapsulate key elements such as measures, dimensions, attributes, facts, relationships, hierarchies, and standard and non-aggregable metrics. By effectively abstracting the underlying data complexities, the solution enables advanced analytical capabilities without necessitating extensive data literacy from users.)
/E (A robust semantic layer is vital for ensuring that all enterprise data is governed by consistent business definitions and metrics. This layer should comprehensively encapsulate key elements such as measures, dimensions, attributes, facts, relationships, hierarchies, and standard and non-aggregable metrics. By effectively abstracting the underlying data complexities, the solution enables advanced analytical capabilities without necessitating extensive data literacy from users.)
