/T (A centralized security framework is essential to ensure consistent enforcement of governance policies across all access points. This framework should feature robust functionalities such as Security Filters, Object Level Access Control \(ACLs\), and Granular User Privileges. Furthermore, it should enable management of user groups and role-oriented permissions, along with flexible authentication protocols to safeguard sensitive information, particularly in the context of interactions with large language models \(LLMs\).)
/E (A centralized security framework is essential to ensure consistent enforcement of governance policies across all access points. This framework should feature robust functionalities such as Security Filters, Object Level Access Control \(ACLs\), and Granular User Privileges. Furthermore, it should enable management of user groups and role-oriented permissions, along with flexible authentication protocols to safeguard sensitive information, particularly in the context of interactions with large language models \(LLMs\).)
