/T (What makes a true semantic layer vs. basic data models: Unlike basic data catalogs or data virtualization tools that primarily expose databases as another database or simply catalog underlying tables, Strategy Mosaic allows analysts and architects to define consistent business definitions and a security model within its layer. It transforms technical data connectivity into business-friendly objects and definitions. While some vendors have semantic layers, these are often not universal, being tied to specific databases or applications. Strategy Mosaic, in contrast, aims to be a universal intelligence layer, decoupling business semantics and security from the underlying data storage.)
/E (What makes a true semantic layer vs. basic data models: Unlike basic data catalogs or data virtualization tools that primarily expose databases as another database or simply catalog underlying tables, Strategy Mosaic allows analysts and architects to define consistent business definitions and a security model within its layer. It transforms technical data connectivity into business-friendly objects and definitions. While some vendors have semantic layers, these are often not universal, being tied to specific databases or applications. Strategy Mosaic, in contrast, aims to be a universal intelligence layer, decoupling business semantics and security from the underlying data storage.)
